# Written to exercise M0 moves. A 3-qubit repetition round whose decoder
# is lowered from a switch into nested if/else: each case applies its
# correction, then resets both ancillas. Under M0 every reset stays core:
# a reset that merges out of the inner If is still inside an outer arm,
# and the outer arms do not match because one side is a nested If.
qubits 5
bits 5
x q0
cx q0 q1
cx q1 q2
h q2
h q2
cx q0 q3
cx q1 q3
cx q1 q4
cx q2 q4
measure q3 -> c3
measure q4 -> c4
if c3 & !c4 {
  x q0
  reset q3
  reset q4
} else {
  if c3 & c4 {
    x q1
    reset q3
    reset q4
  } else {
    if !c3 & c4 {
      x q2
      reset q3
      reset q4
    } else {
      reset q3
      reset q4
    }
  }
}
measure q0 -> c0
measure q1 -> c1
measure q2 -> c2
